WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
Here's a sentence you
could say any evening.

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.020
'I was watching TV':
«Je regardais la télé».

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.050
'When my brother arrived':
«quand mon frère est arrivé».

4
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.190
Both things happened in the past.

5
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.840
Yet the two verbs look nothing alike.

6
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.420
Why does French need two different
past tenses in one short sentence?

7
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.290
In this mission, you'll map a
Saturday at the beach onto a timeline,

8
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.150
sentence by sentence.

9
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.380
Then you'll fill the
missing verbs in a holiday

10
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.210
story and watch the whole thing play.

11
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.780
Your mission: work out
when each past tense fits,

12
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.850
and tell a story that uses both.
